    "text": "A thin strip <math><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> long is on a <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></math> shaped wire of negligible resistance and it is connected to a spring of spring constant <math><mn>0.5</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> (see figure). The assembly is kept in a uniform magnetic field of <math><mn>0.1</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the strip is pulled from its equilibrium position and released, the number of oscillations it performs before its amplitude decreases by a factor of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math> is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> . If the mass of the strip is <math><mn>50</mn></math> grams, its resistance <math><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> and air drag negligible, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> will be close to:<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d72e34f8-3dd4-4ae5-a09d-1dacd793ddec-image.png\" style=\"width: 260px; height: 148px;\" />",
